description:
Location: pkix-path/src/serde_der.rs, option_vec::serialize() (lines 262-295)

The function allocates BOTH a Vec<Vec<u8>> (bytes_buf) and a Vec<String> (str_buf) with capacity equal to the input length, then populates only one of them based on is_human_readable(). The other buffer is allocated but never used.

Rewrite:

  if is_hr {
      let mut str_buf: Vec<String> = Vec::with_capacity(values.len());
      for v in values {
          let der_bytes = v.to_der().map_err(serde::ser::Error::custom)?;
          str_buf.push(Base64::encode_string(&der_bytes));
      }
      serializer.serialize_some(&str_buf)
  } else {
      // ... bytes_buf path ...
  }

What goes wrong: wasted allocation proportional to input length. For small Vec<T> fields this is noise; for a ValidatedPath with many policy qualifiers it is one unnecessary Vec allocation per serialize call.
